1. HYPER Agents IDE (hyper-agents-ide.onrender.com)

What it is: A 3-panel agent control room — agents list left, chat center, skills/tools right. Running on Render (LOCAL / DEV / Port 3500 shown in header).

What's working great:

The layout is clean and professional — instantly readable

The "Train skill" panel with Title / Body / Idempotency key is a solid pattern

"local-echo" agent linked and ready to go

Issues I can see right now:

"Failed to load agents" + "Failed to load chat history" + "Failed to load skills" — the backend isn't fully connected. This is likely a Render cold-start issue or the local server isn't running

Being on Render free tier means cold starts — users will hit this every time

Recommendations:

Move the backend to Railway or Fly.io for persistent uptime — no cold starts

Add a loading skeleton / spinner instead of raw "Failed to load" error messages — it looks broken even when it's just warming up

Add an agent health indicator that auto-retries connection

2. Hyperfocus Z0ne Showcase (showcase-web-omega.vercel.app)

What it is: The main landing/portfolio hub. Showcases the whole ecosystem — HyperCode V2.4, Hyper-Vibe Course, BROski-Obsidian-Brain, BROskiPets dNFT, HyperAgent-SDK. Five repos, one brain.

What's working great:

"Build your AI Brain" headline is strong and memorable

The live status ticker at the bottom (Course: online, HyperCode: running, Agents: testing...) is a brilliant touch — gives it a real "control room" energy

The ecosystem section with LIVE/BETA/WIP badges is super clear

Messaging for ADHD/dyslexic devs is differentiated and honest — "Real builds, not tutorial toys" hits hard

Recommendations:

The gap between the hero section and the "Stop doom-scrolling tutorials" banner feels a bit empty — could fill with a short animated demo or a stats ticker (e.g. "X BROskis minted / X XP earned today")

Add a direct link to the WelshDog HyperCode IDE from the nav — it's arguably your most powerful tool

The "Hyper Station 1.0" demo sounds incredible — it needs its own featured card with a screenshot/video, not buried in the gallery

3. WelshDog HyperCode IDE (127.0.0.1:8088)

What it is: The local powerhouse — a full dashboard with Metrics Home, Services, Agents, Tasks, BROski Pulse, Docker Zone, MCP, Health, Pricing sections. Running locally with impressive depth.

What's working great:

The dashboard layout is genuinely impressive — multi-panel, data-rich, real-time metrics (88 API req/min, 123ms avg response)

Mode switcher at the top (Default / Dyslexia / High-C / Focus) is elite — this is killer UX for your audience

BROski Pulse section with BROski$, XP, Top Agent is a great gamification integration

Navigation depth (Hyper Station, IDE, Agents, Mission, MCP, Docker Zone, Health) shows real maturity

Issues I can see:

System Health showing CRITICAL / trae-ide-trae-ide-1 DOWN — that service needs attention

Error rate at 58.62% is high — worth investigating what's throwing errors

Tasks showing "Could not validate credentials" — auth/token needs reconnecting

0 agents reporting — same connection issue as the Agents IDE

Recommendations:

Fix the trae-ide-trae-ide-1 Docker container — it's marking system health as CRITICAL

Add a one-click "reconnect all" or "restart services" button in the Health panel

The Dyslexia/High-C/Focus modes deserve their own mini onboarding tooltip — new users won't know what these do

Consider making this cloud-deployable (not just localhost) so you can show it off publicly

4. Hyper Vibe Coding Course (hyper-vibe-coding-course.vercel.app)

What it is: Gamified coding course for ADHD/dyslexic/autistic devs. 12 modules, 29 AI agents (Spider, Bee, etc.), XP + BROski$ rewards, dNFT pets, leaderboard. Free to start, no credit card.

What's working great:

The Spider AI mentor bubble ("Want a hint or shall we just ship it? 🚀") is perfect — sets the tone immediately

"Reduce-motion friendly" checkbox is a thoughtful accessibility win

The Vibe Labs (Claude, Google AI Studio, Trae IDE, etc.) are genuinely unique — nobody else has this

12 modules from "first line of code" to "shipped a dNFT pet contract" is an ambitious but compelling arc

Recommendations:

The page was scrolled mid-content when I screenshotted — make sure the hero is always fully visible on first load

Show the leaderboard on the homepage (even a mini top-5) — social proof + FOMO is powerful for your audience

The 29 agents need a dedicated "Meet your mentors" section — people will bond with these characters

Add a "What you'll ship" section with real screenshots of student projects — nothing converts better than proof

